==In animation==
[[File:Tabitha anime.png|thumb|250px|Tabitha in {{aniseries|RS}}]]
===''Pokémon the Series''===
===={{aniseries|RS}}====
Only one Magma Admin, [[Tabitha]], ever appeared in the {{pkmn|animated series}}. He made his debut along with {{tc|Aqua Admin}} [[Shelly]] in ''[[AG027|A Three-Team Scheme]]'', where he was mistakenly referred to as "Field Commander Harlan" in the English [[dub]]; this was corrected in subsequent episodes. He led a squad on a mission to [[Dewford Town|Dewford Island]] to find the [[Cave of Origin]]. It was revealed that he was carrying the [[Blue Orb]] (mistakenly referred to as the "Indigo Orb" in the English dub) with him at the time, though it was never shown onscreen.

Tabitha appeared several other times throughout ''[[Pokémon the Series: Ruby and Sapphire]]'' in command of {{tc|Team Magma Grunt}}s: at the [[Oceanic Museum]] in ''[[AG036|The Spheal of Approval]]'' and at [[Mt. Chimney]] in ''[[AG054|Fight for the Meteorite!]]''. His final appearance was in ''[[AG097|Gaining Groudon]]'' and ''[[AG098|The Scuffle of Legends]]'', where he witnessed the battle between [[Kyogre and Groudon (Ruby and Sapphire series)#Kyogre|Kyogre]] and [[Kyogre and Groudon (Ruby and Sapphire series)#Groudon|Groudon]]. Like the rest of Team Magma, he is not seen again after these episodes.
{{-}}

==In the manga==
[[File:Three Fires.png|thumb|200px|The original Three Fires in Pokémon Adventures]]
===Pokémon Adventures===
===={{MangaArc|Ruby & Sapphire}}====
There are three admins of Team Magma known collectively as the '''Three Fires''' (Japanese:  '''三頭火''' ''Three Head Fires''). [[Courtney#First Courtney|Courtney]] and [[Tabitha#First Tabitha|Tabitha]] are directly based on their game counterparts while [[Blaise]] is exclusive to Pokémon Adventures. They collectively serve as the second-in-commands to [[Maxie]].

The members of the Three Fires has a special memory-recording lighter in the horns of their outfits than can burn the memories of its holder onto paper. The three lighters can also link up and mix their memory data with each other. Each member also utilizes a different aspect of fire, with Tabitha using smoke to incapacitate opponents, Courtney using flames to create fires, and Blaise using heat to cause his opponents to hallucinate.

Throughout the ''Ruby & Sapphire'' arc, the Three Fires succeed in retrieving the [[Scanner]] to locate the [[Red Orb|Red]] and [[Blue Orb]]s and also capture [[Captain Stern]] and his assistant, [[Dock]] in order to obtain the [[Submarine Explorer 1]]. Together with the {{tc|Aqua Admin}}s, they attempt to prevent the Hoenn Gym Leaders from stopping {{p|Kyogre}} and {{p|Groudon}}, though they are ultimately unsuccessful.

In the arc's conclusion, Tabitha and Courtney begin normal lives, whereas Blaise begins a new quest to reawaken Groudon.

===={{MangaArc|Omega Ruby & Alpha Sapphire}}====
Blaise returns to Team Aqua's {{ci|Lilycove}} Headquarters and unexpectedly encounters {{adv|Amber}}. The manga-exclusive counterparts eventually strike a deal to work together, and force {{p|Hoopa}} to summon {{p|Kyogre}} and {{p|Groudon}}, so that they would be able to trace their respective leaders' whereabouts. It is then revealed that "Courtney" and "Tabitha" were merely codenames for the game-based Magma Admins; two characters based on Courtney and Tabitha in {{g|Omega Ruby and Alpha Sapphire}} are introduced as co-operators with [[Zinnia]].
{{-}}

